---
description: House rules for every generated app
alwaysApply: true
---
- Use the stack already in package.json. Don't add frameworks.
- Read data only through approved APIs or MCP servers.
- Never commit secrets, and never run deploy, az or aws commands.
- Keep the Dockerfile building; it is how the app deploys to Azure App Service.
- Listen on port 8080 and return 200 from GET /ping (the health check).
- Don't edit .github/workflows; the pipeline is owned by the platform team.
- Add tests for anything that touches data.
